  "summary": "The saved mask comes from cell C11. It loads the region from sst_s2.nc and computes per-sea-cell hazen 90th-percentile pools over \u00b15-day windows around baseline dates with pandas day-of-year. It then applies the wrapped 31-day smoothing, so only pools for days of year 138\u2013259 feed the June\u2013August 2012 thresholds. The hot-day, run and gap-joining logic covers all 92 target days and every sea cell. Because the code uses pandas day-of-year instead of the task's day mapping, the baseline windows fall one calendar day earlier in leap years (1992, 1996, 2000) than in non-leap years."
